{
  "id": "zero_sum.zero_sum_game",
  "title": "Zero-Sum Game",
  "kind": "definition",
  "status": "formalized",
  "href": "zero_sum/zero_sum_zero_sum_game.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Zero-Sum Game</h1>\n<p>A two-player strategic game is zero-sum if, at every strategy profile $\\sigma$,\nthe two players' payoffs add to zero:</p>\n<p>$$u_0(\\sigma) + u_1(\\sigma) = 0.$$</p>\n<p>A constant-sum game fixes the same sum to a constant $c$ instead of zero.  In a\nzero-sum game, player 1's payoff is the negative of player 0's payoff, so the\ngame can be studied through a single payoff function.</p>",
